{
  "created": "2026-03-30T00:00:00.000Z",
  "id": "vx-vxjs0nex",
  "meta": {
    "description": "VxJSON stores CMS content as git-friendly JSON files with content-last field ordering for 4KB-optimized metadata indexing and deterministic ETags.",
    "title": "VxJSON — Content Storage Format"
  },
  "modified": "2026-04-05T10:45:00.158Z",
  "type": "puck",
  "content": {
    "puckData": {
      "content": [
        {
          "props": {
            "badgeText": "STORAGE FORMAT",
            "buttons": [],
            "description": "Conloca's git-friendly content storage format. Standard JSON with content-last field ordering for fast metadata indexing and deterministic ETags.",
            "id": "Hero-y5z6a7b8",
            "title": "VxJSON"
          },
          "type": "Hero"
        },
        {
          "props": {
            "blockId": "vx-wh4t1svxj",
            "id": "ContentBlockSection-c9d0e1f2",
            "label": "",
            "startsNewSection": "true",
            "subtitle": "VxJSON is standard JSON with a .vxjson extension and two guarantees: the content field is always last, and field order is deterministic. That is it. No special parser needed -- any JSON reader can open a VXJSON file.",
            "title": "What is VxJSON?",
            "tone": "transparent",
            "width": "default"
          },
          "type": "ContentBlockSection"
        },
        {
          "props": {
            "blockId": "vx-whyc0nt3nt",
            "id": "ContentBlockSection-k7l8m9n0",
            "label": "",
            "startsNewSection": "true",
            "subtitle": "By placing the content field last, all metadata fits within the first 4KB of every file. This unlocks two performance advantages.",
            "title": "Why Content-Last?",
            "tone": "transparent",
            "width": "default"
          },
          "type": "ContentBlockSection"
        },
        {
          "props": {
            "blockId": "vx-cr4shs4f3",
            "id": "ContentBlockSection-s5t6u7v8",
            "label": "",
            "startsNewSection": "true",
            "subtitle": "Every file write in Conloca uses an atomic write strategy. Content is written to a temporary file first, then atomically renamed to the target path. This is a Conloca runtime feature -- independent of the VxJSON format -- ensuring the original file is never corrupted if the process crashes mid-write.",
            "title": "Crash-Safe Writes",
            "tone": "transparent",
            "width": "default"
          },
          "type": "ContentBlockSection"
        },
        {
          "props": {
            "blockId": "vx-3t4gc0ncur",
            "id": "ContentBlockSection-a3b4c5d6",
            "label": "",
            "startsNewSection": "true",
            "subtitle": "Every VXJSON file carries a dual-format ETag that prevents stale overwrites when multiple editors work simultaneously. The format is:",
            "title": "ETag Concurrency",
            "tone": "transparent",
            "width": "default"
          },
          "type": "ContentBlockSection"
        },
        {
          "props": {
            "blockId": "vx-st4l3wr1t3",
            "id": "ContentBlockSection-i1j2k3l4",
            "label": "",
            "startsNewSection": "true",
            "subtitle": "When an editor saves, the CMS sends the expected ETag. If the file was modified since it was loaded, the server rejects the write with a STALE_WRITE error and presents a conflict resolution dialog. No content is silently overwritten.",
            "title": "",
            "tone": "transparent",
            "width": "default"
          },
          "type": "ContentBlockSection"
        },
        {
          "props": {
            "badgeText": "",
            "buttons": [
              {
                "href": "/getting-started/",
                "id": "btn-vx-1",
                "label": "Get Started",
                "variant": "primary"
              },
              {
                "href": "/",
                "id": "btn-vx-2",
                "label": "Back to Home",
                "variant": "secondary"
              }
            ],
            "id": "CTABanner-m5n6o7p8",
            "subtitle": "Get started with Conloca and see how VxJSON keeps your content safe, versioned, and git-friendly.",
            "title": "See it in action"
          },
          "type": "CTABanner"
        }
      ],
      "root": {
        "props": {}
      },
      "zones": {}
    }
  }
}
